<title>UK: John Lewis UK store sales up 10.9% in latest week.</title>
<headline>John Lewis UK store sales up 10.9% in latest week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The John Lewis Partnership  JLP.CN said its UK department store sales rose 10.9 percent in the week to February 22 compared with the same week a year earlier.</p>
<p>In the four weeks to February 22 sales were up 9.5 percent.</p>
<p>Total sales, including those from the Waitrose supermarket chain, rose 8.3 percent in the week and were up 6.9 percent in the four-week period.</p>
<p>-- Richard Murphy, London Newsroom 44 171 542 2774</p>
